{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the consequences that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick wit and sharp dialogue. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, which chronicles the rise of facebook from a college dorm room to a global phenomenon.\n\nthe movie follows the story of mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a harvard student who creates a website called facemash, which becomes an instant hit on campus. however, the site also gets him into trouble, and he is eventually approached by a group of students, including twins cameron and tyler winklevoss, who want him to create a social networking site for harvard students.\n\nmark agrees to work on the site, but he soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it with his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield. as the site gains popularity, mark and eduardo become wealthy and famous, but they also attract the attention of the winklevoss twins, who claim that mark stole their idea.\n\nthe movie explores the themes of friendship, loyalty, and the consequences of success. mark's relationship with eduardo is particularly noteworthy, as it is portrayed as a complex and nuanced one. the two friends are initially close, but as facebook becomes more successful, they begin to drift apart.\n\nthe film also explores the theme of class and privilege, as mark and his friends navigate the complex social hierarchy of harvard. the movie suggests that mark's success is not just due to his intelligence and hard work, but also to his ability to navigate the social norms of the elite.\n\nthe acting in the movie is superb, with jesse eisenberg giving a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake is memorable as sean parker, the co-founder of napster.\n\nthe direction by david fincher is also noteworthy, as he brings a sense of style and sophistication to the film. the cinematography is sleek and modern, and the score by trent reznor and atticus ross is haunting and atmospheric.\n\noverall, the social network is a fascinating and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of success and the consequences of ambition. it is a movie that will appeal to anyone who is interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it, and it is a must-see for anyone who loves great storytelling and exceptional filmmaking.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0297507643699646}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.004086359404027462}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.35463178157806396}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0001971527235582471}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.6843717098236084}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.005940163973718882}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.01826760545372963}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00022575691400561482}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.4740769863128662}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " consequences", "logprob": -1.084902048110962}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -4.6967357775429264e-05}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.015844985842704773}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.537788011773955e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0015391181223094463}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.1739863157272339}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.0796213150024414}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0